# Flutter Architecture – AskmeHUMG

## Folder Structure

```
lib/
├── app/
│   ├── core/
│   │   ├── error/          # failures.dart, exceptions.dart
│   │   ├── network/        # firebase_providers.dart
│   │   ├── providers/      # theme_provider.dart
│   │   └── values/         # colors, spacing, theme, typography, assets
│   ├── global_widgets/     # AppButton, AppCard, AppAvatar, etc.
│   ├── services/           # api_client.dart
│   └── modules/
│       └── <feature>/
│           ├── domain/     # entity, i_repository, use_cases  ← flat, no sub-folders
│           ├── data/       # model, datasource, repository_impl  ← flat, no sub-folders
│           └── presentation/
│               ├── <feature>_providers.dart  ← all providers in one file
│               └── screens/
├── config/                 # bootstrap, di, router, languages, app_routes
├── generated/              # flutter_gen output (do not edit)
└── l10n/                   # ARB files + generated localizations
```

Each layer has files directly — no sub-folders inside `domain/`, `data/`.

## Layer Rules
- `domain/` — pure Dart only, no Flutter/Firebase imports
- `data/` — all Firebase calls live here
- `presentation/` — no direct Firestore calls; use providers

## State Management – Riverpod 3.x

```dart
@riverpod
class AuthNotifier extends _$AuthNotifier {
  @override
  FutureOr<void> build() {}

  Future<void> signIn() async {
    state = const AsyncLoading();
    state = await AsyncValue.guard(
      () => ref.read(signInWithGoogleProvider).call(),
    );
  }
}

// In widget
ref.watch(authNotifierProvider);     // watch in build()
ref.read(authNotifierProvider.notifier).signIn();  // read in callbacks
```

## Freezed 3.x — always `abstract class`

```dart
@freezed
abstract class AuthUser with _$AuthUser {
  const factory AuthUser({required String uid}) = _AuthUser;
}
```

## Global Widgets — AppButton

Always use `AppButton` with a variant instead of creating a new button widget:

```dart
AppButton(label: l10n.authSignInWithGoogle, variant: AppButtonVariant.google, onPressed: ...)
```

Current variants: `primary`, `secondary`, `ghost`, `danger`, `google`.

## Type-safe assets (flutter_gen)

```dart
// ✅ Use generated Assets.* — never hardcode asset paths
Assets.imagesAppIcon.image(width: 180, height: 180)
Assets.svgsGoogleLogo.svg(width: 20, height: 20)

// ❌ Never hardcode
// Image.asset('assets/images/app_icon.png')
// SvgPicture.asset('assets/svgs/google_logo.svg')
```

## Naming Conventions

| Type | Pattern | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Screen | `*Screen` | `LoginScreen` |
| Providers file | `<feature>_providers.dart` | `auth_providers.dart` |
| Notifier | `*Notifier` | `AuthNotifier` |
| Repository interface | `I*Repository` | `IAuthRepository` |
| Repository impl | `*RepositoryImpl` | `AuthRepositoryImpl` |
| Use cases file | `<feature>_use_cases.dart` | `auth_use_cases.dart` |

## Localization
All user-facing strings must use `AppLocalizations.of(context).*` — never hardcode display strings.

## Theme Colors
Always use `Theme.of(context).colorScheme.*` — never hardcode colors directly.
